    36→ * {@code DataInput} may only be used from one thread, because it is not thread safe (it keeps internal state like file position).
    37→ * To allow multithreaded use, every {@code DataInput} instance must be cloned before used in another thread. Subclasses must
    38→ * therefore implement {@link #clone()}, returning a new {@code DataInput} which operates on the same underlying resource, but
    39→ * positioned independently.
